.he "df (1)                       3/18/82                       df (1)"  
.fo "                               -#-" 
.in 5
.rm 65
.bd
PROGRAM
.br
.in +5
.bd
df
- disk free space


.in -5
.bd
USAGE        
.br
.in +5
.bd
df [device ...]


.in -5
.bd
FUNCTION   
.br
.in +5
.bd
Df
prints the free and used blocks and inodes of each filesystem.
With no argument, every mounted filesystem is reported; a named
device is reported whether mounted or not, and may be given with
or without a "/dev/" prefix.

This command is somewhat analogous to the CP/M STAT command.


.in -5
.bd
EXAMPLE
.br
.in +5
.bd
df /dev/root

.in -5
.bd
SEE ALSO
.br
.in +5
dcheck (1), icheck (1), ncheck (1), fsck (1)
